Done. Completed **T043** — propagating correlation through the lifecycle export path.

**What was missing:** The agent-export path (orchestrator → `proposer.sh` → `agent_stream.py`) already forwarded the full correlation identity (`feature/role/phase/attempt/invocation`). But the lifecycle path — `wiggum_emit`, which every `run_start`/`phase_start`/`reject`/`run_stop`/etc. event goes through — only carried `run_id/task/backend`. That left lifecycle events unqueryable by `feature` (FR-032) and without trace correlation (FR-033).

**Changes (both files T043 names):**
- `wiggum-lib.sh` — `wiggum_emit` now emits an ambient `feature` field on every lifecycle event, plus an optional `trace_id` **only when `WIGGUM_TRACE_ID` is set**. Trace context is passed through, never synthesized, so local recording never depends on a trace existing.
- `orchestrator.sh` — exports the resolved (sanitized) feature `SLUG` as `WIGGUM_FEATURE` and passes through any inbound `WIGGUM_TRACE_ID`, alongside the existing correlation exports.

The Loki/OTLP `--json-stdin` path already flattens arbitrary event fields, so these reach both sinks with no change to the T040/T041 shipper files.

**Verified:**
- `bash -n` clean on all four shell scripts.
- Manual `wiggum_emit` run confirms `feature` is always present, `trace_id` appears only with a trace set, and output stays valid JSON.
- Full `lib` suite: 279 passed.

